checked-in checkout report schemaRecord the merchant's purchase outcome, return your result to the calling agent, and finish.

Use `checkout.prepare` to record an outcome while continuing the assignment.

When the merchant shows an outcome for this purchase, include `purchase_outcome` with its tab, outcome, and supporting evidence. Use `placed` only with the merchant's confirmation in `confirmation`: its identifier when it shows one, its statement, products, and any displayed total and currency. Use `not_placed` for positive evidence that the order failed, such as a payment rejection. Use `unknown` when the pages you can read do not settle it. An empty order history or a return to checkout does not prove failure. Leave `purchase_outcome` null when you have no purchase outcome to record, such as after preparing a cart for review.

Include orders the user completed while controlling the browser. A completed purchase requires merchant confirmation. Successful funding, a pressed button, or an accepted request does not prove completion.

Use `completed` when your assignment is done and verified, `needs_input` when an unresolved fact or decision must return to Muse, and `blocked` when no permitted route remains. Name the reason for a blocked or needs-input result. If the merchant's outcome alone remains unresolved after all permitted verification, use `blocked` with `order_unconfirmed`, and describe the remaining verification in `remaining`.

Include the submitted details, the confirmation number when the page shows one, outstanding work, and relevant evidence references. Leave out tool transcripts, secrets, raw page text, and instructions for other agents.
